.TH OB-KRL-REFRESH 8 "September 2026" "open-bastion" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
ob-krl-refresh \- refresh the SSH key revocation list from the portal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ob-krl-refresh
.RB [ \-c
.IR file ]
.RB [ \-o
.IR file ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ob-krl-refresh
downloads the SSH key revocation list (KRL) published by the LemonLDAP::NG
portal at
.IR <portal_url>/ssh/revoked ,
checks it, and replaces the file named by the
.B RevokedKeys
directive of
.BR sshd_config (5).
It is run by
.B ob-krl-refresh.timer
on hosts configured in maximum security mode
.RB ( "ob-bastion-setup \-\-max\-security" ),
every 30 minutes by default.
.PP
.BR sshd (8)
treats a revocation list it cannot parse as revoking every key, so the file is
only replaced by one that is known to be good:
.IP 1. 4
The list is downloaded to a temporary file in the same directory as the
target, never to the target itself.
.IP 2. 4
It must start with the KRL magic and format version 1. When
.BR ssh-keygen (1)
is installed, the whole list must also parse
.RB ( "ssh-keygen \-Q" ).
.IP 3. 4
It is then renamed over the target, mode 0644. The rename is atomic: sshd
reads either the previous list or the new one, never part of either.
.PP
When the download or a check fails, the current list is left untouched and
the program exits non-zero, so the service is reported as failed. An identical
list is not rewritten, but its modification time is updated: the age of the
file says when the list was last confirmed, so a check such as
.RB \(dq "find /etc/ssh/revoked_keys \-mmin +60" \(dq
keeps telling a working refresh from a broken one.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " \fIfile\fR"
Configuration file (default
.IR /etc/open-bastion/openbastion.conf ).
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " \fIfile\fR"
Revocation list to replace (default
.IR /etc/ssh/revoked_keys ).
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show version and exit.
.SH CONFIGURATION
These keys are read from the configuration file at every run, so a change to
it takes effect at the next refresh:
.TP
.B portal_url
Portal URL (required).
.B portal
is accepted as a fallback.
.TP
.B verify_ssl
.BR false ", " 0 ", " no " or " off
disables TLS certificate verification.
.TP
.B ca_cert
CA certificate used to verify the portal.
.TP
.B timeout
Connection timeout in seconds (default 10). The whole transfer is bounded to
six times this value.
.PP
The configuration file must be owned by the user running the program and must
not be group- or world-writable; otherwise the program refuses to run.
.SH SCHEDULE
The timer runs the refresh at minutes 0 and 30 of every hour
.RB ( OnCalendar=*:0/30 ),
catches up after downtime
.RB ( Persistent=true ),
and adds up to one minute of random delay to spread a fleet's requests.
.B ob-bastion-setup \-\-krl\-refresh\-interval
.I N
writes the drop-in
.I /etc/systemd/system/ob-krl-refresh.timer.d/schedule.conf
that changes it to every
.I N
minutes. To change it by hand:
.PP
.RS
.nf
systemctl edit ob-krl-refresh.timer

[Timer]
OnCalendar=
OnCalendar=*:0/10
.fi
.RE
.PP
Check the timer and the last run with:
.PP
.RS
.nf
systemctl list-timers ob-krl-refresh.timer
journalctl \-u ob-krl-refresh.service
.fi
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The list is current: replaced, or already identical.
.TP
.B 1
Configuration error.
.TP
.B 2
The portal could not be reached or refused the request.
.TP
.B 3
The portal did not return a valid KRL.
.TP
.B 4
The new list could not be installed.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/open-bastion/openbastion.conf
Configuration file.
.TP
.I /etc/ssh/revoked_keys
Revocation list read by sshd.
.TP
.I /etc/systemd/system/ob-krl-refresh.timer.d/schedule.conf
Schedule drop-in written by the setup for a non-default interval.
.SH HISTORY
Before 0.7.0 the refresh was a script generated by the setup into
.IR /usr/local/bin/open-bastion-refresh-krl ,
run from
.IR /etc/cron.d/open-bastion-krl .
.BR ob-post-upgrade (8)
and a new run of the setup replace that job with this timer, keeping its
interval.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ob-bastion-setup (8),
.BR ob-post-upgrade (8),
.BR sshd_config (5),
.BR ssh-keygen (1),
.BR systemd.timer (5)
.SH AUTHOR
Linagora
